# Shared launch handover

For Iron Compass launch and app/website integration work, automatically read
`C:/Users/adamf/.codex/.chatgpt-projects/g-p-6ac72dbaf0ac81918f6d28d7785c40c3/LAUNCH-HANDOFF.txt`
at the start of a task and after switching branches/checkouts. Follow its linked
current integration checklist and verified status when relevant. Do not repeat
full historical audits. Repository facts and newer human instructions take
precedence over stale checkpoint claims.

Before editing a repository, inspect HEAD and dirty state and read applicable
instructions. Preserve unrelated changes. If another agent is editing the same
checkout/files, do independent read-only work until ownership is resolved.

At a meaningful milestone and before your final reply, reread the shared handover
and update only CURRENT HANDOVER with: Brisbane timestamp, assistant, checkout,
branch/full SHA, local versus pushed/deployed state, exact changed files, relevant
checks and results, blocker/approval status, and one next action. Read-only work
also deserves a checkpoint when it establishes a new material fact. Do not claim
pass from old evidence or overwrite another assistant's newer work. If the file
is unavailable, report that fact; do not claim progress was synchronized.

Keep credentials, tokens, private member content and tax/bank data out of handovers.
No production writes, commits, deployment-triggering pushes, releases, purchases,
paid services, metered/saved QA reviews, account changes, or irreversible actions
without the owner's applicable approval. Normal local inspection and focused
preparation may continue; no new features, large audits or automated paid Cursor
execution. Do not reset quotas or edit original member records as tests.

This rule maintains file-based continuity during agent turns. It is not a
background service, live chat bridge or guarantee of execution after a crash,
quota exhaustion, closed editor or interruption before checkpointing.
